@startuml dispatch-lifecycle
!theme plain
title v0.3: provision an agent, then start one execution (dispatch = both + retire on exit)

participant "Caller" as C
participant "swarma-dispatcher\n(swarma-dispatcher)" as D
participant "swarma-user-manager" as H
participant "swarma-credential-broker" as B
participant "Supervisor" as S
participant "swarma-user-launcher" as L
participant "curator-run narrow exec mode\n(agent account; first broker consumer)" as E

== provision ==
C -> C : compose immutable plan and resolved PATH; digest on caller side
C -> D : provision {request_id: R, accounts, …, grants, auth: {key, sig}}
note over C,D
  Signed domain: swarma-dispatcher request/1 + newline + CCJ-1 without auth.
  Root (caller principal, R) is correlation, not each downstream key.
end note
D -> D : reconcile first; prepare: principal ↔ key, signature,\ncaller chain (agent.spawn, credential.lease, depth ≥ 1),\nquotas, constructible leaf; write input/1
alt refused
  D --> C : error {code}
else accepted
  alt capacity gate closed
    alt v0
      break capacity refusal
        D --> C : refuse capacity:* (no provisioning or start)
      end
    else v1
      D --> C : queued handle
      ... capacity opens ...
      D -> D : dequeue re-checks authority and all gates
    end
  end
  group only after owned capacity claim admitted
    D -> H : user.create {kind: agent, label, request_id: E-create}
    H --> D : {uid, generation}
    D -> D : sign leaf agent:<generation> = request ∩ caller ∩ own grant
    D -> B : bind {lease chain, caller chain, intersection, request_id: E-bind}
    B --> D : binding_id
    D --> C : agent/1 {agent_id, state: idle}
  end
end
note over D,B
  Quota/authority failures never queue in either version.
  E-create and E-bind are distinct derived effect IDs (§4.5).
  Proceed to start only for an admitted idle allocation.
end note
== start ==
C -> D : start {request_id: R-start, agent_id, plan, plan_digest, auth}
note over C,D
  Separate provision/start commands have separate root IDs.
  A combined dispatch uses one root R for both halves (§4.5).
end note
D -> D : re-check authority and lifetime; owned execution capacity claim\n(v0 refusal / v1 queue); claim {execution_id, epoch}
D -> S : start supervisor
S -> D : registered (pid, start time) — durable ack
S -> L : no-argument sudo launcher; stdin launch.start\n{request_id: E-launch, generation, execution_id, epoch, executor, plan}
L -> L : validate generation, approved executor, home;\nwrite start receipt while root (pid, start time, boot id)
L -> E : reset environment/descriptors; clear groups; set GID/UID;\nexec (immutable plan on FD3; no inherited broker connection)
S -> D : receipt recorded → running
E -> E : verify caller-composed plan; no compose/profile resolution;\nprepare work dir in agent home; protected binding
E -> B : open own connection; lease (caller dependency re-checked)
E -> E : qualified injection; exec harness
note over L,E
  Versioned intake / Decision 0021 amendment must be published and qualified.
  Narrow exec mode has no network except broker; harness egress is separate.
end note
... running ...
alt cancel or max_runtime
  S -> H : exec.stop {request_id: E-stop, generation, execution_id}
  H --> S : termination receipt (no process of the execution remains)
else exit
  E --> S : exit status
end
S -> D : outcome; allocation idle (or retiring for dispatch)
opt dispatch on-exit cleanup or allocation retirement
  D -> B : unbind {request_id: E-unbind, …}
  B --> D : confirmed
  D -> H : user.retire {request_id: E-retire, home: archive | delete, …}
  H --> D : account retirement confirmed
  opt keeper integration active and identity registered as one-shot
    D -> D : separate identity revocation effect after retirement; confirm via keeper
  end
  note over D,H
    Standing identities: operator-only signed revocation.
    Terminal only after applicable cleanup effects confirmed.
    Unknown effects stay pending and retry with their own same ID (§7).
  end note
end
@enduml
